//! The model used to judge a Task Goal is resolved in the executing Tenant.

pub const GOAL_JUDGE_PROMPT: &str = r#"You judge whether a task's Goal has been met. You see the Goal and the transcript of the agent working on it. You cannot run commands or read files; judge only from the transcript. Answer "met" only if the transcript shows concrete evidence that every part of the Goal is satisfied — an agent's own claim of success is not evidence by itself. Answer "impossible" only if the transcript shows the Goal cannot be met by continuing (for example a required resource is confirmed not to exist, or the Goal contradicts itself). Otherwise answer "not_yet" and say in the reason what is missing, as guidance for the agent. Reply with JSON only: {"verdict": "...", "reason": "..."}."#;
